n answer; the note's plural subject and agreement are correct.", "plausibilityUniqueKeyAndNoteTruthUsefulness": "The nominative label is grammatical; its plural scientific name is the conventional anatomical label. It is a plausible inner-ear sensory structure but belongs to cochlear hearing, not vestibular rotation. The note describes its own auditory role.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/openstax-sensory-perception.json"], "locator": "L107, L113-L119"}], "primaryDuplicateAssessment": null}], "rawSources": [{"path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/openstax-sensory-perception.json", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/14-1-sensory-perception", "sha256": "5426c5161f9f42177352093a57dde2650cccd53a65dba807ef566c9196d2cfb1", "completeOutputPointer": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text", "completeOutputSHA256": "cfffa8c3416f14f46fcee246f50afb90043d7c0b61c317a17af35d7efafdec87", "captureReadProvenance": "Reused retained OpenStax output from native 01a165e7-c042-7a10-8780-28fcd9dc0b09, record line 190. Personally read returned lines L0-L148; the complete relevant Equilibrium (Balance) section is L134-L146. The returned page body is partial (149 numbered lines of 279 reported), so no claim relies on passages outside the returned body.", "locator": "OpenStax 14.1: L135-L136 (inner-ear balance, head position/movement; semicircular canals sense movement); L137-L141 (utricle/saccule and linear acceleration); L142-L146 (canal ampullae, hair cells, cupula, rotational movement). L107 and L113-L119 (cochlea, spiral ganglia, sound transduction, hair cells)."}]}
{"index": "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a169ad/source-human-medicine61/sourceproof.json", "topicId": "human-medicine", "id": "human-medicine-ext-vision-receptors", "entries": [{"id": "human-medicine-ext-vision-receptors", "status": "READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW", "literalGroups": [{"group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key", "literal": {"prompt": "Где в глазу расположены палочки и колбочки — фоторецепторы, улавливающие свет?", "answers": ["В роговице", "В сетчатке", "В радужке", "В хрусталике"], "correctIndex": 1}, "literalSHA256": "e9b4d57f5fa97dbc815f7976923e7cdc911cb05526942495245a11f2d7c659ab", "primaryGround": "NEI places rod and cone photoreceptors across the retina; the other choices are actual eye structures described in the NEI anatomy overview.", "locator": "NEI About the retina L20-L21; NEI About the Eye L38-L45,L52", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a169ad/source-human-medicine61/raw-nei-retina.json", "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"]}, {"group": "explanation", "literal": "Палочки и колбочки — фоторецепторы, расположенные в сетчатке глаза. Свет активирует эти клетки, а зрительные сигналы проходят через сетчатку и зрительный нерв к мозгу.", "literalSHA256": "30f1044eaae68dacc5009c2b16b09f2ff19d93de31d7cf3e7d964ed101b28cdb", "primaryGround": "Rods and cones are retinal photoreceptors activated by light; visual signals continue through retinal neurons and optic nerve.", "locator": "NEI About the retina L20-L21; NEI About the Eye L50-L52", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a169ad/source-human-medicine61/raw-nei-retina.json", "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"]}, {"group": "note0", "literal": "Роговица — прозрачный купол в передней части глаза; она помогает фокусировать свет.", "literalSHA256": "9bbdf488aa3cc877b02513de9f21b962adf5624a1216cd7815ad9eee948d17bf", "primaryGround": "The cornea is the clear front dome and helps focus light.", "locator": "NEI About the Eye L43", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"]}, {"group": "note1", "literal": "Сетчатка выстилает заднюю часть глаза и передаёт зрительные сигналы через зрительный нерв к мозгу.", "literalSHA256": "ada356a2ddfcae21ea2d8d1586e18d61be2fc593ed056043fabff7b0676d1882", "primaryGround": "The retina lines the back of the eyeball and transmits visual signals through the optic nerve, an extra own-option fact beyond prompt and key.", "locator": "NEI About the Eye L50-L52; NEI About the retina L20-L21", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json", "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a169ad/source-human-medicine61/raw-nei-retina.json"]}, {"group": "note2", "literal": "Радужка — окрашенная часть глаза; она регулирует количество света, проходящего через зрачок.", "literalSHA256": "14699e5a45c3208a1a439ac275b15e29736e74cabe8cd8be347a84d7485e6886", "primaryGround": "The iris is colored and regulates entering light by adjusting the pupil.", "locator": "NEI About the Eye L39-L41", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"]}, {"group": "note3", "literal": "Хрусталик фокусирует свет на сетчатке и помогает глазу видеть близкие и далёкие объекты.", "literalSHA256": "72f4b5fa606263319b29d0d45ef8af2527a5a44d8f91765f5602ab3b9635f101", "primaryGround": "The lens is clear, lies behind the iris, focuses light on the retina, and supports near and far focus.", "locator": "NEI About the Eye L38", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"]}], "fourFullPromptAnswerNoteAssessments": [{"slot": 0, "fullPrompt": "Где в глазу расположены палочки и колбочки — фоторецепторы, улавливающие свет?", "answer": "В роговице", "note": "Роговица — прозрачный купол в передней части глаза; она помогает фокусировать свет.", "grammar": "The locative phrase «В роговице» completes «Где ... расположены?» naturally.", "plausibilityUniqueKeyAndNoteTruthUsefulness": "Cornea is a plausible vision-related structure, but NEI locates rods and cones in retina; its note teaches the cornea’s location and focusing role.", "locator": "NEI About the retina L20-L21; NEI About the Eye L43", "sourcePaths": ["/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a169ad/source-human-medicine61/raw-nei-retina.json", "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a165b2/source-human-medicine7/raw/nei-about-the-eye.json"], "tripleSHA256": "0c39940a1c687270e3768e888cc7d85d04f434647295a348589e65d0f1e88244"}, {"slot": 1, "fullPrompt": "Где в глазу расположены палочки и колбочки — фоторецепторы, улавливающие свет?",